00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:00.000
all right, don't fuss."

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:09.730
"All right, don't fuss!" rumbled the cars.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:14.950
Thomas began going faster and faster.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:22.150
He whistled as he rushed through Henry's tunnel.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:31.660
"Hurry, hurry," called Thomas.

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:33.760
He was feeling very proud of himself,

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:39.400
but the cars grew crosser and crosser.

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:43.060
Last, Thomas slowed down as he came to Gordon's Hill.

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:07.650
"Steady now, steady," warned the driver as they reached the top.

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:09.310
He began to put on the brakes.

00:23:09.310 --> 00:23:12.510
"We're stopping, we're stopping," called Thomas.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:17.390
"No, no, no," answered the cars, bumping into each other.

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:19.530
"Go on, go on."

00:23:19.530 --> 00:23:24.210
Before the driver could stop them, they had pushed Thomas down the hill and were rattling

00:23:24.210 --> 00:23:26.720
and laughing behind him.

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:30.000
Poor Thomas tried hard to stop them from making him go too fast.

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:32.550
"Stop pushing! Stop pushing!" he hissed.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:34.550
But the cars took no notice.

00:23:34.550 --> 00:23:37.970
"Go on! Go on!" they giggled in their silly way.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:46.850
"Where's the station? Oh dear, what shall I do?" he cried.

00:23:46.850 --> 00:23:49.990
They rattled straight through and swerved into the goodyard.

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:53.010
Thomas shut his eyes. "I must stop!"

00:23:56.340 --> 00:24:00.000
When he opened his eyes, he saw he had stopped just in front of the buffers.

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:06.170
There watching him was Sir Topham Hatton.

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:13.560
"What are you doing here, Thomas?" he asked.

00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:17.090
"I've brought Edward's freight cars," Thomas answered.

00:24:17.090 --> 00:24:18.910
"Why did you come so fast?"

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:21.890
"I didn't mean to. I was pushed," said Thomas.

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:26.020
"You've got a lot to learn about freight cars, Thomas.

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:30.000
"After pushing them about here for a few weeks, you'll know almost"

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.420
as much about them as Edward.

00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:34.970
Then you'll be a really useful engine.

00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:54.050
Story, it was just what I needed.

00:25:02.490 --> 00:25:06.260
Stacey, did you put that entire schedule together for memory?

00:25:06.260 --> 00:25:09.410
Well, I had some help from Mr. Conductor.

00:25:09.410 --> 00:25:10.650
Mr. Conductor?

00:25:10.650 --> 00:25:13.120
He lives in the wall.

00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:15.840
Oh, yes. The little man who lives in the wall.

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:16.710
I forgot.

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:20.750
Wait, is that right?

00:25:20.750 --> 00:25:26.440
You mean I can catch the train at 20 after and still be in Mount Careful before the other train?

00:25:26.440 --> 00:25:29.800
Yes, it's the new train that's stopping here today.

00:25:30.350 --> 00:25:33.190
Wow, that's wonderful. I won't be late at all.

00:25:34.050 --> 00:25:35.870
Say, what are you kids doing with those instruments?

00:25:36.240 --> 00:25:39.910
We're going to meet the new train. We're going to play for the passengers.

00:25:40.810 --> 00:25:41.930
Well, may I join you?

00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:44.920
If you really want to, you can play with us.

00:25:45.060 --> 00:25:48.540
Would I like to, but I'd love to. I'll be right back.

00:25:48.540 --> 00:25:59.570
Do-do-do-do! Do-do-do!

00:26:00.250 --> 00:26:13.040
Sound of a one-man band.

00:26:13.410 --> 00:26:13.790
Oh.

00:26:16.720 --> 00:26:26.060
There's a one-man band convention at Mount Careful,

00:26:26.300 --> 00:26:29.880
and I'm the only participant, and I didn't want to miss it.

00:26:30.320 --> 00:26:32.890
I'm sorry that I seem so upset before.

00:26:32.890 --> 00:26:35.080
I should have taken time to read the schedule.

00:26:35.080 --> 00:26:38.480
Well, no, I should have taken time to get it right the first time.

00:26:38.480 --> 00:26:41.980
And from now on, I'm keeping a pad and pencil right by the phone

00:26:41.980 --> 00:26:44.920
so I don't make that same mistake again.

00:26:44.920 --> 00:26:48.830
New train pulling in!

00:26:48.830 --> 00:26:53.470
I've been thinking, like, maybe Tex could become a one-man band.

00:26:53.470 --> 00:26:56.770
Oh, considering how long it's taken both Rex and Tex

00:26:56.770 --> 00:26:59.570
to learn just one half of the guitar each,

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:00.990
"Forget it."

00:27:03.620 --> 00:27:08.320
"Listen, he's playing. Let's all join in."

00:27:39.950 --> 00:27:59.700
little guy wheels on the wall for the speed reach for the whistle go where the rail may run reach for the world

00:28:00.190 --> 00:28:11.850
